{"url": "https://www.last.fm/music/Lorde/_/Homemade+Dynamite", "tags": ["Tove Lo", "synthpop", "pop", "electropop", "dance-pop"], "wiki": {"content": "“Homemade Dynamite” is the third track on Lorde’s sophomore album Melodrama, which dropped on June 16, 2017. Lorde teamed up with Tove Lo in her LA “Gingerbread House” Max Martin studio—complete with a mattress-walled vocal booth—to craft the song, which she calls the point in the night when “everyone's at a good level and maybe the sharp edges of the evening haven't quite shown themselves yet.” 

Lorde described it as a “bootleg” sample turned “shiny pop mix” that broke away from the album’s breakup theme to celebrate friendship and euphoric energy. In a Coachella 2017 debut, she introduced it as reflecting “the good, crazy part of living in your twenties.” She has also defended her interpretive dance performance of the song at the 2017 MTV VMAs done while having the flu and unable to sing. She told Marc Maron that “it’s sort of embarrassing to watch someone experience intense joy,” which may explain why some viewers found it “disconcerting,” but she felt authentically herself. <a href="http://www.last.fm/music/Lorde/_/Homemade+Dynamite">Read more on Last.fm</a>. User-contributed text is available under the Creative Commons By-SA License; additional terms may apply.", "summary": "“Homemade Dynamite” is the third track on Lorde’s sophomore album Melodrama, which dropped on June 16, 2017. Lorde teamed up with Tove Lo in her LA “Gingerbread House” Max Martin studio—complete with a mattress-walled vocal booth—to craft the song, which she calls the point in the night when “everyone's at a good level and maybe the sharp edges of the evening haven't quite shown themselves yet.” 

