{"track": {"url": "https://www.last.fm/music/Timbaland/_/The+Way+I+Are", "mbid": "00833a9a-0545-42ee-a39d-3e25df9dd4b1", "name": "The Way I Are", "wiki": {"content": ""The Way I Are" is a song by record producer Timbaland featuring singer-songwriter Keri Hilson & rapper D.O.E., released on June 12, 2007 as the second single from Timbaland's second album Shock Value and also included on international editions of Keri's debut album In a Perfect World... (2009). The 2 artists co-wrote the song with Danja, The Clutch, and Candice Nelson. Timbaland also produced the song, along with Danja co-producing. The Way I Are is an electrohop song with influences of R&B and dance music that help create it's futuristic sound. It's lyrics are based on the theme of role reversal and sensual desires, Timbaland explains that he is flat broke, while Hilson replies that she does not care about any of that, and jokes that she can pay him to strip.

The music video for the song was directed by Shane Drake and was filmed in Salford, United Kingdom on May 18, 2007. Shane commented on the video and said: "I like to tell stories with my videos — and Timbaland's new video is going to be unlike any other. Utilizing the tools of incendiary cinematography and fierce lighting schemes, I plan to sculpt an edgy masterpiece, oozing with style and impact. With each rhythmic pulse and beat we will time crafty edits, sharp as tacks and smooth as steel. This video is going to be an artistic expression of Timbaland's music. As an added element of force and velocity, we will follow Timbaland as he cruises around the city. From the colors like pink and blue, to the wardrobe — to the edits, we will craft a slick masterpiece that defies genre and truly defines cool & will show off Timbaland in a "super" music video". The video version of the song includes an extra verse from Timbaland's brother Sebastian. This verse was added to 'pad out' the song, as the album version of the song has an elongated period of time in which nothing but the beat is played. Though being unusual for American music video productions, the video world premiered and received its first official airing on June 15 on the German music television channel VIVA. The video also includes 3 British freestyle football players. A "director's cut" of the video is now on YouTube and it features Timbaland in a black cab and shows him in a more casual perspective. The music video has received over 700 million views on YouTube.

The Way I Are debuted at #99 on the Billboard Hot 100 on the week of June 9, 2007. After about a month of climbing it leaped from #40 to #18 & from there reached the top 10 for the first time, rising from #18 to #6 on the week of July 14, 2007 and marked Timbaland's second top 10 single as a lead artist following #1 hit "Give It To Me" featuring Nelly Furtado & Justin Timberlake, it was also the first top 10 for both Keri Hilson & D.O.E. The Way I Are soon reached it's peak of #3 for 4 non-consecutive weeks in August, September & October 2007 after remaining stable in the top 10 & an increase in radio airplay becoming the chart's "Greatest Airplay Gainer" around that time. The Way I Are reached the summit of the U.S. Billboard Pop Songs on the issue dated September 15, 2007, and stayed there for 3 consecutive weeks. The Way I Are ranked #18 on the Billboard Hot 100 Year-End list of 2007 as well as ranking #4 on the 2000s decade on the Pop Songs chart compiled by Billboard. The Way I Are is currently certified 3× Platinum by the RIAA. <a href="http://www.last.fm/music/Timbaland/_/The+Way+I+Are">Read more on Last.fm</a>. User-contributed text is available under the Creative Commons By-SA License; additional terms may apply.", "summary": ""The Way I Are" is a song by record producer Timbaland featuring singer-songwriter Keri Hilson & rapper D.O.E., released on June 12, 2007 as the second single from Timbaland's second album Shock Value and also included on international editions of Keri's debut album In a Perfect World... (2009). The 2 artists co-wrote the song with Danja, The Clutch, and Candice Nelson. Timbaland also produced the song, along with Danja co-producing. The Way I Are <a href="http://www.last.fm/music/Timbaland/_/The+Way+I+Are">Read more on Last.fm</a>.", "published": "16 Feb 2009, 17:19"}, "album": {"url": "https://www.last.fm/music/Timbaland/Shock+Value", "image": [{"size": "small", "#text": "https://lastfm-img.freetls.fastly.net/i/u/34s/483ee6586f4704ee5d478071540ec0d7.png"}, {"size": "medium", "#text": "https://lastfm-img.freetls.fastly.net/i/u/64s/483ee6586f4704ee5d478071540ec0d7.png"}, {"size": "large", "#text": "https://lastfm-img.freetls.fastly.net/i/u/174s/483ee6586f4704ee5d478071540ec0d7.png"}, {"size": "extralarge", "#text": "https://lastfm-img.freetls.fastly.net/i/u/300x300/483ee6586f4704ee5d478071540ec0d7.png"}], "title": "Shock Value", "artist": "Timbaland"}, "artist": {"url": "https://www.last.fm/music/Timbaland", "mbid": "daa09819-5da5-4c7a-8bef-eb372bb27ff1", "name": "Timbaland"}, "toptags": {"tag": [{"url": "https://www.last.fm/tag/Timbaland", "name": "Timbaland"}, {"url": "https://www.last.fm/tag/Hip-Hop", "name": "Hip-Hop"}, {"url": "https://www.last.fm/tag/dance", "name": "dance"}, {"url": "https://www.last.fm/tag/rnb", "name": "rnb"}, {"url": "https://www.last.fm/tag/pop", "name": "pop"}]}, "duration": "179000", "listeners": "1772915", "playcount": "16223601", "streamable": {"#text": "0", "fulltrack": "0"}}}

