Along with the announcement, the band dropped the two lead singles, "Complainer" and "4th of July." The first takes on a person we all know, who talks the talk but doesn't necessarily walk the walk. "Now you're out on your own, don't know where you belong/Don't sit around and complain about it/You say you want to change this world/Don't sit around and complain about it," the hook rings in the upbeat, funky tune. The latter takes a more sentimental tone, reminiscing on easy summer nights.  <a href="http://www.last.fm/music/Cold+War+Kids/_/Complainer">Read more on Last.fm</a>. User-contributed text is available under the Creative Commons By-SA License; additional terms may apply.", "summary": "It's been two years since Cold War Kids' last album, 2017's LA Divine, and now the boys are back, announcing their next effort, NEW AGE NORMS.   

